6. Article 182 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, manipulates the trading prices of securities or futures, thereby obtaining illegitimate interests or transferring risks, shall, if the circumstances are serious, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains:
(1) manipulating the trading prices of securities or futures by, alone or in collusion with others, concentrating capital advantages, shareholding or position holding advantages, or using information advantages to jointly or continuously buy or sell;
(2) colluding with another person to engage in securities or futures transactions with each other at a prearranged time, price, and manner, or buying from or selling to each other securities not held, thereby affecting the trading prices or trading volumes of securities or futures;
(3) taking oneself as the counterparty to conduct self-buying and self-selling of securities without transferring ownership of the securities, or taking oneself as the counterparty to self-buy and self-sell futures contracts, thereby affecting the trading prices or trading volumes of securities or futures;
(4) manipulating the trading prices of securities or futures by other means.
"Where a unit commits the crime mentioned in the preceding paragraph, a fine shall be imposed on the unit, and the persons who are directly in charge and the other persons who are directly responsible for the crime shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention."
